# Normalize line endings for ordinary text so every platform (Windows dev
# machines, Linux CI runners, zip exports) checks out the same bytes. This is
# what tests/test_source_documents_unchanged.py needs: that test hashes raw
# file bytes, so any tool that silently rewrites line endings on checkout
# would break it even though nothing in the repository actually changed.
#
# Deliberately `text=auto` with NO `eol=` here: `text`/`eol` are independent
# per-path attributes, and a later `-text` override (below) only unsets
# `text` - it does NOT clear an `eol=lf` set by this blanket rule, so a
# blanket `eol=lf` would still force LF onto vn.txt on checkout even with
# `-text` set (confirmed with `git check-attr -a vn.txt` after a first,
# wrong attempt at this file: `eol: lf` was still showing). Omitting `eol=`
# here means there is nothing for vn.txt's rule below to fail to override.
* text=auto

# vn.txt predates this convention and is committed with CRLF line endings -
# its sha256 hash is pinned in tests/test_source_documents_unchanged.py.
# -text means "never normalize this file's line endings, under any platform
# or tool" - the one safe way to keep an already-hashed file byte-identical
# forever, rather than trying to make a normalization rule match a hash it
# was never computed against.
vn.txt -text

# Explicit binary - avoids relying on git's own content-sniffing heuristics
# for files whose integrity also matters (source documents, generated art).
*.docx -text
*.png -text
*.webp -text
*.woff -text
*.woff2 -text
